cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Fault-Tolerance Scaffold Simulator: Hardware Errors, Measurement Errors, and Software Decoding"
authors:
  - family-names: Kiefer
    given-names: Boris
    affiliation: "New Mexico State University"
    email: bkiefer@nmsu.edu
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0242-3165"
version: v2.0
date-released: 2026-06-01
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/boriskiefer/fault-tolerance-scaffold-simulator"
abstract: >
  A classical repetition-code simulator that introduces the systems logic
  of fault tolerance through hardware errors, measurement errors, and
  majority-vote software decoding. Version 2.0 adds a multi-cycle
  error-correction model, a three-panel interactive figure covering
  majority-vote curves, operating region heatmap, and resource estimation,
  and a companion guided exercises document with pre- and post-exercise
  questions and answers.
keywords:
  - fault tolerance
  - quantum error correction
  - repetition code
  - majority vote
  - quantum computing education
  - error threshold
  - resource estimation
  - logical qubit
